`AutomergeConflictValue` represents a value returned by conflict-aware methods like `GetAll`, `Values`, `ListRange`, and `MapRange`. When multiple peers concurrently write to the same key or index, Automerge picks a winner deterministically but preserves all concurrent values. `AutomergeConflictValue` provides access to both winning and losing values along with their operation IDs.

```csharp
using Ray.Automerge;

var values = doc.GetAll(root, "status");
foreach(var v in values)
{
  if(v.IsObject)
    Console.WriteLine($"Object: {v.ObjectId} ({v.ObjectType})");
  else
    Console.WriteLine($"Scalar: {v.Scalar?.Kind} (op: {v.OperationId})");
}
```

# AutomergeConflictValue

```csharp
public sealed class AutomergeConflictValue
```

A value entry that may be part of a conflict. Contains either a scalar value or an object reference, along with the operation ID that produced it.

**Namespace:** `Ray.Automerge`

## Properties

### IsObject

```csharp
public bool IsObject { get; }
```

Whether this value is a container (Map, List, or Text). When `true`, use `ObjectId` and `ObjectType`. When `false`, use `Scalar`.

### Scalar

```csharp
public AutomergeScalarValue? Scalar { get; }
```

The scalar value. Non-null when `IsObject` is `false`. See [AutomergeScalarValue](/Ray.Toolkit.Automerge/api/automerge-marks/#automergescalarvalue) for the value type details.

### ObjectId

```csharp
public AutomergeObjectId? ObjectId { get; }
```

The object ID of the container. Non-null when `IsObject` is `true`.

### ObjectType

```csharp
public AutomergeContainerType? ObjectType { get; }
```

The container type (Map, List, or Text). Non-null when `IsObject` is `true`.

### OperationId

```csharp
public string OperationId { get; }
```

The operation ID that created this value. Format: `"counter@actorId"`. Useful for debugging conflicts and understanding which peer wrote which value.

# Methods That Return Conflict Values

These `AutomergeDocument` methods return `IReadOnlyList` of `AutomergeConflictValue`:

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `GetAll(objectId, key)` | All concurrent values at a map key |
| `GetAll(listId, index)` | All concurrent values at a list index |
| `GetAllAtHeads(objectId, key, heads)` | Historical concurrent values at a map key |
| `GetAllAtHeads(listId, index, heads)` | Historical concurrent values at a list index |
| `Values(objectId)` | All values in a map or list |
| `ValuesAtHeads(objectId, heads)` | Historical values in a map or list |
| `MapRange(mapId, startKey, endKey)` | Values in a key range |
| `MapRangeFull(mapId)` | All values in a map |
| `ListRange(listId, start, end)` | Values in an index range |
| `ListRangeFull(listId)` | All values in a list |

# Detecting Conflicts

A key or index has a conflict when `GetAll` returns more than one entry:

```csharp
var values = doc.GetAll(root, "color");
if(values.Count > 1)
{
  Console.WriteLine($"Conflict! {values.Count} concurrent values:");
  foreach(var v in values)
  {
    Console.WriteLine($"  {v.Scalar?.StringValue} from op {v.OperationId}");
  }
  // The first entry is the "winner" — the value returned by GetString etc.
}
else if(values.Count == 1)
{
  Console.WriteLine($"No conflict: {values[0].Scalar?.StringValue}");
}
```

# Reading Values from Conflict Entries

```csharp
var values = doc.GetAll(root, "data");
foreach(var v in values)
{
  if(v.IsObject)
  {
    // Value is a nested container
    var containerType = v.ObjectType; // Map, List, or Text
    var id = v.ObjectId;
    // Use id with doc.GetKeys, doc.ListLength, doc.GetText, etc.
  }
  else
  {
    // Value is a scalar
    var scalar = v.Scalar!;
    switch(scalar.Kind)
    {
      case AutomergeScalarValueKind.String:
        Console.WriteLine(scalar.StringValue);
        break;
      case AutomergeScalarValueKind.Int:
        Console.WriteLine(scalar.IntValue);
        break;
      case AutomergeScalarValueKind.Boolean:
        Console.WriteLine(scalar.BoolValue);
        break;
      case AutomergeScalarValueKind.Null:
        Console.WriteLine("null");
        break;
      // ... handle other kinds
    }
  }
}
```

# See Also

- [AutomergeScalarValue](/Ray.Toolkit.Automerge/api/automerge-marks/#automergescalarvalue) — Scalar value details
- [Conflict Values Guide](/Ray.Toolkit.Automerge/guides/conflicts/conflict-values/) — Working with conflicts
- [Detecting Conflicts Guide](/Ray.Toolkit.Automerge/guides/conflicts/detecting-conflicts/) — Identifying concurrent writes
- [AutomergeDocument — GetAll](/Ray.Toolkit.Automerge/api/automerge-document/#getall-map) — Conflict-aware read methods","src/content/docs/api/automerge-conflicts.mdx","636ed7e9a8e9d148","api/automerge-cursor",{"id":39,"data":41,"body":47,"filePath":48,"digest":49,"deferredRender":23},{"title":42,"description":43,"editUrl":23,"head":44,"template":33,"sidebar":45,"pagefind":23,"draft":16},"AutomergeCursor","API reference for AutomergeCursor — stable position tracking in lists and text",[],{"hidden":16,"attrs":46},{},"# Overview

`AutomergeCursor` represents a stable position reference in a List or Text container. Unlike numeric indices that shift when elements are inserted or removed, a cursor tracks a logical position that follows the element it was anchored to, even as concurrent edits change the surrounding content.

Cursors are created via `AutomergeDocument.GetCursor` and resolved back to an index via `AutomergeDocument.GetCursorPosition`.

```csharp
using Ray.Automerge;

using var doc = AutomergeDocument.Create();
var textId = doc.PutObject(doc.RootId, "content", AutomergeContainerType.Text);
doc.SpliceText(textId, 0, 0, "Hello world");

// Create a cursor at position 5 (the space)
var cursor = doc.GetCursor(textId, 5);

// After edits, resolve the current position
doc.SpliceText(textId, 0, 0, "Say: "); // Insert before cursor
var pos = doc.GetCursorPosition(textId, cursor); // 10 (shifted right by 5)
```

# When to Use Cursors

Cursors solve the "moving target" problem in collaborative editing:

- **Text editor selections** — Track where a user's caret is positioned across remote edits
- **Bookmarks** — Mark a specific location in a list or text that persists through changes
- **Annotations** — Anchor comments or highlights to specific content
- **Undo targets** — Remember where an operation occurred for undo/redo

Without cursors, you would need to manually adjust indices every time a remote peer inserts or deletes content before your position.

# Methods

## FromBytes

```csharp
public static AutomergeCursor FromBytes(ReadOnlySpan<byte> bytes)
```

Creates a cursor from its serialized byte representation. Use this to restore a cursor that was previously serialized with `ToBytes`.

**Parameters:**
- `bytes` — The serialized cursor data.

**Returns:** A restored `AutomergeCursor`.

```csharp
byte[] saved = File.ReadAllBytes("cursor.bin");
var cursor = AutomergeCursor.FromBytes(saved);
```

## ToBytes

```csharp
public byte[] ToBytes()
```

Serializes the cursor to a byte array. The result can be persisted and later restored with `FromBytes`.

**Returns:** A byte array containing the serialized cursor data.

```csharp
byte[] data = cursor.ToBytes();
File.WriteAllBytes("cursor.bin", data);
```

# Creating Cursors

Cursors are created through `AutomergeDocument.GetCursor`:

```csharp
public AutomergeCursor GetCursor(AutomergeObjectId objectId, ulong index)
```

**Parameters:**
- `objectId` — The List or Text object.
- `index` — The current index to anchor the cursor to.

**Returns:** An `AutomergeCursor` tracking that position.

# Resolving Cursors

Cursors are resolved through `AutomergeDocument.GetCursorPosition`:

```csharp
public ulong GetCursorPosition(AutomergeObjectId objectId, AutomergeCursor cursor)
```

**Parameters:**
- `objectId` — The List or Text object the cursor belongs to.
- `cursor` — The cursor to resolve.

**Returns:** The current index position, accounting for all changes since the cursor was created.

# Complete Example

```csharp
using var doc = AutomergeDocument.Create();
var root = doc.RootId;
var textId = doc.PutObject(root, "content", AutomergeContainerType.Text);

// Write some text
doc.SpliceText(textId, 0, 0, "The quick brown fox");
doc.Commit("initial text");

// Create a cursor at "brown" (position 10)
var cursor = doc.GetCursor(textId, 10);

// Serialize the cursor for storage
byte[] cursorBytes = cursor.ToBytes();

// Simulate concurrent edits that shift indices
doc.SpliceText(textId, 0, 0, ">>> "); // Insert 4 chars at start
doc.Commit("prefix");

// Restore and resolve the cursor
var restored = AutomergeCursor.FromBytes(cursorBytes);
var newPos = doc.GetCursorPosition(textId, restored);
// newPos is 14 — the cursor followed "brown" through the shift

var text = doc.GetText(textId);
// text is ">>> The quick brown fox"
// Position 14 still points to 'b' in "brown"
```

# Cursors with Lists

Cursors work with List containers too:

```csharp
var listId = doc.PutObject(root, "items", AutomergeContainerType.List);
doc.ListInsertString(listId, 0, "alpha");
doc.ListInsertString(listId, 1, "beta");
doc.ListInsertString(listId, 2, "gamma");

// Cursor at "beta" (index 1)
var cursor = doc.GetCursor(listId, 1);

// Insert before "beta"
doc.ListInsertString(listId, 0, "zero");

// Cursor still points to "beta"
var pos = doc.GetCursorPosition(listId, cursor); // 2
var value = doc.ListGetString(listId, pos); // "beta"
```

# Cursor Persistence

Cursors are lightweight byte arrays that can be stored alongside documents. A common pattern is to persist cursor positions with the document state:

```csharp
// Save document and cursor together
byte[] docData = doc.Save();
byte[] cursorData = cursor.ToBytes();

// Later: restore both
using var loaded = AutomergeDocument.Load(docData);
var loadedCursor = AutomergeCursor.FromBytes(cursorData);
var position = loaded.GetCursorPosition(textId, loadedCursor);
```

# See Also

- [AutomergeDocument — GetCursor / GetCursorPosition](/Ray.Toolkit.Automerge/api/automerge-document/#getcursor) — Creating and resolving cursors
- [Cursors Guide](/Ray.Toolkit.Automerge/guides/text/cursors/) — Conceptual guide to collaborative cursor tracking","src/content/docs/api/automerge-cursor.mdx","bff03ae88ac82339","api/automerge-document",{"id":50,"data":52,"body":58,"filePath":59,"digest":60,"deferredRender":23},{"title":53,"description":54,"editUrl":23,"head":55,"template":33,"sidebar":56,"pagefind":23,"draft":16},"AutomergeDocument","Complete method reference for AutomergeDocument — the core class for creating, reading, and writing Automerge CRDT documents",[],{"hidden":16,"attrs":57},{},"# Overview

`AutomergeDocument` is the primary class for working with Automerge CRDT documents. It provides methods for creating documents, reading and writing data, managing history, synchronizing with peers, and persisting state.

The class implements `IDisposable` because it holds a native Rust resource. Always use a `using` statement.

```csharp
using Ray.Automerge;

using var doc = AutomergeDocument.Create();
```

# Creation and Disposal

## Create

```csharp
public static AutomergeDocument Create(string? actorId = null)
```

Creates a new empty Automerge document.

**Parameters:**
- `actorId` — Optional actor identifier. If null, a random actor ID is generated. If a valid hex string, it is used directly as the Automerge actor. If a non-hex string, it is UTF-8 encoded and used as the actor bytes.

**Returns:** A new `AutomergeDocument`.

**Exceptions:**
- `AutomergeException` — If the actor ID is invalid.

```csharp
using var doc = AutomergeDocument.Create();
using var docWithActor = AutomergeDocument.Create("my-app-device-1");
```

## Load

```csharp
public static AutomergeDocument Load(byte[] data)
```

Loads a document from binary data produced by `Save`.

**Parameters:**
- `data` — The binary document data. Must not be null or empty.

**Returns:** A new `AutomergeDocument` containing the loaded state.

**Exceptions:**
- `ArgumentNullException` — When `data` is null.
- `ArgumentException` — When `data` is empty.
- `AutomergeException` — When the data is invalid or corrupted.

```csharp
byte[] saved = originalDoc.Save();
using var restored = AutomergeDocument.Load(saved);
```

## LoadWithOptions

```csharp
public static AutomergeDocument LoadWithOptions(byte[] data, LoadOptions options)
```

Loads a document with configurable verification and error handling.

**Parameters:**
- `data` — The binary document data. Must not be null or empty.
- `options` — Load configuration. See `LoadOptions`.

**Returns:** A new `AutomergeDocument`.

**Exceptions:**
- `ArgumentNullException` — When `data` or `options` is null.
- `ArgumentException` — When `data` is empty.
- `AutomergeException` — When the data is invalid.

```csharp
var options = new LoadOptions
{
  VerificationMode = VerificationMode.NoCheck,
  OnPartialLoad = OnPartialLoad.Ignore
};
using var doc = AutomergeDocument.LoadWithOptions(saved, options);
```

## Dispose

```csharp
public void Dispose()
```

Releases the native Automerge document. Automatically rolls back any uncommitted changes before disposal to prevent native panics.

## RootId

```csharp
public AutomergeObjectId RootId { get; }
```

Gets the root object ID. Every document has a root Map container where top-level data is stored.

**Exceptions:**
- `ObjectDisposedException` — When the document has been disposed.

```csharp
var root = doc.RootId;
doc.PutString(root, "title", "My Document");
```

## ActorId

```csharp
public string ActorId { get; set; }
```

Gets or sets the actor identifier for this document. The actor ID identifies who made changes and is important for synchronization.

When getting: returns the human-readable string if the hex can be decoded to printable UTF-8, otherwise returns the raw hex.

When setting: hex strings are used directly; non-hex strings are UTF-8 encoded.

**Exceptions:**
- `ArgumentException` — When setting to null or whitespace.
- `AutomergeException` — When the value is invalid.

```csharp
doc.ActorId = "user-alice-device-1";
var actor = doc.ActorId;
```

## PendingOperations

```csharp
public ulong PendingOperations { get; }
```

Gets the number of uncommitted operations. Returns 0 after a `Commit` or `Rollback`.

# Commit and Rollback

## Commit

```csharp
public string? Commit(string? message = null, long? timestampMillis = null)
```

Commits all pending operations as a single change.

**Parameters:**
- `message` — Optional commit message describing the change.
- `timestampMillis` — Optional Unix timestamp in milliseconds. If null, Automerge uses its default.

**Returns:** The change hash as a lowercase hex string, or null if there were no pending operations.

```csharp
doc.PutString(root, "title", "Hello");
var hash = doc.Commit("Set title");
```

## Rollback

```csharp
public ulong Rollback()
```

Discards all uncommitted operations and returns the number of operations rolled back.

**Returns:** The number of operations that were rolled back.

```csharp
doc.PutString(root, "title", "mistake");
var count = doc.Rollback(); // count = 1, change discarded
```

## EmptyChange

```csharp
public string EmptyChange(string? message = null, long? timestampMillis = null)
```

Creates a commit with no operations. Useful for creating a merge point or recording metadata.

**Parameters:**
- `message` — Optional commit message.
- `timestampMillis` — Optional timestamp.

**Returns:** The change hash as a lowercase hex string.

# Map Operations

## PutString

```csharp
public void PutString(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, string value)
```

Sets a string value at the given key in a Map container.

**Parameters:**
- `objectId` — The target Map object.
- `key` — The property key.
- `value` — The string value to store.

```csharp
doc.PutString(root, "name", "Alice");
```

## GetString

```csharp
public string? GetString(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Gets a string value from a Map container.

**Parameters:**
- `objectId` — The target Map object.
- `key` — The property key.

**Returns:** The string value, or null if the key does not exist or the value is not a string.

```csharp
var name = doc.GetString(root, "name"); // "Alice"
var missing = doc.GetString(root, "nonexistent"); // null
```

## PutImmutableString

```csharp
public void PutImmutableString(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, ImmutableString value)
```

Sets an immutable string value. Stored identically to `PutString`, but signals that the value should be replaced atomically rather than merged character-by-character. Use for URLs, IDs, and enum-like constants.

## GetImmutableString

```csharp
public ImmutableString? GetImmutableString(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Gets an immutable string value. Returns null if the key does not exist or the value is not a string.

## PutBoolean

```csharp
public void PutBoolean(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, bool value)
```

Sets a boolean value at the given key.

## GetBoolean

```csharp
public bool? GetBoolean(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Gets a boolean value. Returns null if the key does not exist or the value is not a boolean.

## PutInt64

```csharp
public void PutInt64(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, long value)
```

Sets a 64-bit signed integer value at the given key.

## GetInt64

```csharp
public long? GetInt64(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Gets a 64-bit signed integer value. Returns null if the key does not exist or the value is not an integer.

## PutUInt64

```csharp
public void PutUInt64(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, ulong value)
```

Sets a 64-bit unsigned integer value at the given key.

## GetUInt64

```csharp
public ulong? GetUInt64(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Gets a 64-bit unsigned integer value. Returns null if the key does not exist or the value is not an unsigned integer.

## PutDouble

```csharp
public void PutDouble(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, double value)
```

Sets a double-precision floating-point value at the given key.

## GetDouble

```csharp
public double? GetDouble(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Gets a double-precision floating-point value. Returns null if the key does not exist or the value is not a double.

## PutBytes

```csharp
public void PutBytes(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, ReadOnlySpan<byte> value)
```

Sets a byte array value at the given key.

## GetBytes

```csharp
public byte[]? GetBytes(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Gets a byte array value. Returns null if the key does not exist or the value is not bytes.

## PutNull

```csharp
public void PutNull(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
```

Sets an explicit null value at the given key.

## PutCounter

```csharp
public void PutCounter(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key, long value)
```

Sets a CRDT counter at the given key with an initial value. Counters support concurrent increments from multiple peers without conflicts.

## GetCounter

```csharp
public long? GetCounter(AutomergeObjectId objectId, string key)
